## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine basic structures (arrays/deque, hashmap, heap) to maintain a sliding window’s frequency distribution and extract top-K on demand.

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window maintenance with a deque
- Frequency counting via a hashmap
- Min-heap with lazy deletions for top-K
- Amortized update and top-K retrieval costs

## Code Example
```javascript
class SlidingWindowTopK {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W
    this.window = [] // acts as deque (push is at end, shift from start)
    this.counts = new Map()
    this.heap = [] // min-heap of [freq, value]
  }
  _pushHeap(pair) { /* heap push for [freq, value] */ }
  add(x) {
    this.window.push(x)
    this.counts.set(x, (this.counts.get(x) || 0) + 1)
    // push updated freq
    this._pushHeap([this.counts.get(x), x])
    if (this.window.length > this.W) {
      const y = this.window.shift()
      const f = (this.counts.get(y) || 0) - 1
      if (f <= 0) this.counts.delete(y)
      else this.counts.set(y, f)
      this._pushHeap([f, y])
    }
  }
  topK(K) {
    const res = []
    const seen = new Set()
    const pulled = []
    while (res.length < Math.min(K, this.counts.size) && this.heap.length) {
      const [freq, val] = this._popHeap()
      if (!this.counts.has(val) || this.counts.get(val) !== freq) continue
      if (!seen.has(val)) {
        seen.add(val)
        res.push(val)
        pulled.push([freq, val])
      }
    }
    // restore elements for future calls
    for (const p of pulled) this._pushHeap(p)
    return res
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests combining shortest-path DP on DAGs with path counting and reconstruction, using a topological order. It also touches large-number handling and edge case ties.

## Key Concepts
- DAG dynamic programming, topological sort, shortest paths in DAGs, path counting, reconstruction.

## Code Example
```javascript
function countShortestPaths(n, edges, s, t) {
  const adj = Array.from({ length: n }, () => [])
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0)
  for (const e of edges) { const {u,v,w} = e; adj[u].push([v,w]); indeg[v]++ }
  const q = []
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) if (indeg[i]===0) q.push(i)
  const topo = []
  while (q.length) { const u = q.shift(); topo.push(u); for (const [v] of adj[u]) if (--indeg[v]===0) q.push(v) }
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY
  const dist = Array(n).fill(INF); dist[s]=0
  const cnt = Array(n).fill(0); cnt[s] = 1
  const par = Array(n).fill(-1)
  for (const u of topo) {
    for (const [v,w] of adj[u]) {
      const nd = dist[u] + w
      if (nd < dist[v]) { dist[v] = nd; cnt[v] = cnt[u]; par[v] = u }
      else if (nd === dist[v] && dist[u] !== INF) { cnt[v] += cnt[u]; if (par[v] === -1) par[v] = u }
    }
  }
  const path = []
  if (dist[t] !== INF) {
    for (let x = t; x !== -1; x = par[x]) path.push(x)
    path.reverse()
  }
  return { dist: dist[t], count: cnt[t], path }
}
```

